From 170773acd993706362e52ab53e70a3da5d0e2db3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 03:39:17 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 21/60] Lane host halt: a stop's drain deadline ends the rounds
 at the next boundary, and every request queued, filling or running fails with
 the reason.

Opened.halt (optional) lets a server stop an engine between rounds instead of
under a running one; LaneHost.halt is that hook for lane-host families. A
request still filling its prompt a chunk a round fails too, with its lane
freed, and a prompt pass the halt cancels mid-chunk reports the halt's reason
rather than a cancel.

(cherry picked from commit 361f06340a9c9aafb529ee8b172aeb8eb84dde70)
